Port the Apertus 1.5 multimodal model (swiss-ai/vllm apertus-1-5, upstream
PR #50496) to the v0.31.0 APIs. The branch merges without conflicts but was
written against older ones, and the engine failed at startup (jobs 3672072,
3672141):

    TypeError: BaseMultiModalProcessor.__init__() got an unexpected keyword
    argument 'cache'
    TypeError: AutoWeightsLoader.__init__() got an unexpected keyword
    argument 'skip_prefixes'

- Processor: the renderer now tokenizes the prompt and the HF processor sees
  only the media. The processor no longer takes a cache, _call_hf_processor
  takes (hf_data, hf_kwargs), and the tokens-only hook is gone. Apertus HF
  needs one placeholder per media item in its text, so _get_hf_mm_text
  supplies the dummy builder's placeholder text; the per-item crop is
  unchanged.
- Weights: AutoWeightsLoader lost skip_prefixes (#53106). Apertus 1.5 skipped
  only lm_head with tied embeddings, which __init__ already rejects, so it
  loads like upstream ApertusForCausalLM.

